quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  18,5,"They have no knowledge about this, nor did their forefathers. It is a grievous utterance that comes out of their mouths, and they say nothing but a lie."
  18,6,"Yet (O Prophet), perhaps you will consume yourself with grief for their sake if they do not believe in this message (i.e. the Qur’an)."
  18,7,"Indeed, We have made whatever is on the earth an adornment for it, that We may test them as to which of them is best in conduct."
  18,8,And We shall surely turn whatever is upon it into a barren plain.
  18,9,(O Prophet!) Have you considered that the Companions of the Cave and the Valley of al-Raqim (or Inscription) were among Our wonderful signs?*
  18,10,"When the youths took refuge in the cave, they said: ‘Our Lord! Grant us mercy from Your presence and make us incline to the right course concerning our affair.’"
  18,11,So We cast (a veil) over their ears (causing them to fall dead asleep) in the cave for several years.
  18,12,Then We raised them (again) so that We may show (them) which of the two groups had better calculated the period they had stayed (in the cave).
  18,13,"We relate their story to you exactly (as it happened). They were (pious) youths who believed in their Lord, and We increased them in guidance."
  18,14,"We fortified their hearts when they stood up boldly (before their king). They said: ‘Our Lord is the Lord of the heavens and the earth. We will never worship any (false) god besides Him, for then we shall have certainly said an outrageous thing."
  18,15,These people of ours have taken gods besides Him. Why do they not bring any clear evidence to support them? So who could be more unjust than someone who fabricates a lie against Allah?’
